WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.834
-I thought about you
during the Super Bowl.

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:04.234
-Oh, really?
-Do you know why?

00:00:04.234 --> 00:00:05.934
Do you remember?
We did a photo shoot.

00:00:05.934 --> 00:00:08.267
-Our photo shoot, yes.
-You do.

00:00:08.267 --> 00:00:10.200
You're acting like
you don't remember.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.701
-No, I remember.

00:00:11.701 --> 00:00:15.667
-"Yeah, of course.
I remember who you are, Jeremy.

00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:19.267
You're my favorite program.
'The Light Night Show.'"

00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:22.067
-No, yeah, I remember it.

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:24.234
It's hard to remember because
I could barely recognize you.

00:00:24.234 --> 00:00:26.734
Then I kind of found out
at the end it was you.

00:00:26.734 --> 00:00:30.067
-They painted my face. You
can't even tell it's me at all.

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:31.801
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.801 --> 00:00:34.434
That's my face there.
-Yep.

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:35.934
-I mean,
it could have been anyone.

00:00:35.934 --> 00:00:37.667
I mean it doesn't
even look like a person.

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:40.467
-And you were jumping around.
You were screaming.

00:00:40.467 --> 00:00:43.334
We were by this random
hot-dog stand.

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:47.267
They were like, "Just don't
react to anything he's doing."

00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:48.968
-That's right. I remember that.

00:00:48.968 --> 00:00:51.167
I was trying to make you laugh,
though, right?

00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:52.834
-Yes, you were,
and I was, you know,

00:00:52.834 --> 00:00:54.734
just trying to do my job,
not react.

00:00:54.734 --> 00:00:56.734
-I know.
I was getting you in trouble.

00:00:56.734 --> 00:01:00.234
A lot of people don't even
realize when you are a model

00:01:00.234 --> 00:01:02.067
and you do these shoots,
they're tough.

00:01:02.067 --> 00:01:04.067
They're long.
And they're like -- I mean --

00:01:04.067 --> 00:01:06.100
They have you standing
on the edge of a thing

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:07.901
and doing these poses,
but you got to hold it for --

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:09.167
It's almost torture.
It really --

00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:11.234
-Yeah, they're like, "Stand in
the cold. Stand on this rock."

00:01:11.234 --> 00:01:13.667
-That's why I would never, ever
be a model, so don't even --

00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:15.601
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:01:15.601 --> 00:01:17.734
No, I thought we were going to
do so many more shoots together.

00:01:17.734 --> 00:01:21.067
-No, no.
My career is down the drain.

00:01:21.067 --> 00:01:22.400
But I will say this.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:25.234
The "Sports Illustrated"
Swimsuit Issue. The 2018.

00:01:25.234 --> 00:01:29.300
Look at this thing.
This photo of you. Ooh, la, la.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:30.868
I mean, but this is -- Yeah.

00:01:30.868 --> 00:01:32.834
And it just -- Everything
was perfect and gorgeous.

00:01:32.834 --> 00:01:34.968
But tell me the
behind-the-scenes of this one.

00:01:34.968 --> 00:01:37.434
-Yeah, well, we were trying

00:01:37.434 --> 00:01:39.300
to catch "The Little Mermaid"
wave, right?

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:40.634
-Yeah.
-And I think we did.

00:01:40.634 --> 00:01:43.334
-Oh, totally. Yeah. This is
"The Little Mermaid" I remember.

00:01:43.334 --> 00:01:45.801
Yeah. Absolutely. Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.801 --> 00:01:47.534
I remember seeing it
at an odd theater,

00:01:47.534 --> 00:01:49.334
but it was --

00:01:49.334 --> 00:01:52.501
Absolutely, I remember, yes.
-Yeah, so, they --

00:01:52.501 --> 00:01:55.667
-I only saw about 20 minutes
of it, but it was perfect.

00:01:55.667 --> 00:01:57.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.033
-They're like,
"Jump on this rock."

00:01:59.033 --> 00:02:00.767
-Yes.

00:02:00.767 --> 00:02:03.300
-And they're like,
"Again, don't pay attention

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:06.467
to anything happening around you
and just look at the camera."

00:02:06.467 --> 00:02:09.767
So when the big wave was coming,
they were like,

00:02:09.767 --> 00:02:12.734
"Don't look at the wave. Look at
us. Look at us. Look at us."

00:02:12.734 --> 00:02:14.934
So I'm looking at them.
-Trying to be professional.

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:16.601
-Yes, of course. Always.
-As always.

00:02:16.601 --> 00:02:18.534
You got this shot.
But wait till you see --

00:02:18.534 --> 00:02:21.400
We have video footage of what
happened to you on this rock.

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:23.534
Here's Kate Upton at the
"Sports Illustrated" shoot.

00:02:23.534 --> 00:02:25.167
Look at this.

00:02:25.167 --> 00:02:26.534
-Walk the board out.
Watch the spill-out.

00:02:26.534 --> 00:02:28.434
-Watch the spill-out!

00:02:28.434 --> 00:02:30.367
-That's amazing!

00:02:30.367 --> 00:02:32.000
Oh, my God!

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.300
Oh! [Bleep] [Bleep] [Bleep]

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.400
-Grab her. Grab her.
-Oh, my God.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:39.167
-And then here's you laughing.

00:02:39.167 --> 00:02:41.534
Okay, good. You're laughing.
You're fine. But, oh, my God.

00:02:41.534 --> 00:02:43.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:43.434 --> 00:02:44.868
That's frightening.

00:02:44.868 --> 00:02:47.834
-Yeah, it was --
It was really scary.

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:51.934
And, you know,
that moment when the wave hit,

00:02:51.934 --> 00:02:53.467
you just -- I lost all control.

00:02:53.467 --> 00:02:55.734
And luckily, you know,
you saw that man ran up.

00:02:55.734 --> 00:02:58.400
He ran up and grabbed my arm,
and he gave me just enough time

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:01.434
to push off the rock
with my foot.

00:03:01.434 --> 00:03:03.734
So I was able to push
my body away from the rock,

00:03:03.734 --> 00:03:06.400
and it wasn't going to
be a whole face thing.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:09.334
-I mean, that's so frightening,
but I liked that you didn't

00:03:09.334 --> 00:03:11.133
worry about covering
anything up.

00:03:11.133 --> 00:03:12.400
-No, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:15.601
Whenever it's life or death,
you free the nipple.

00:03:15.601 --> 00:03:18.000
-Yeah, absolutely.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.767
Wow. Yeah. I always say that.

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:22.334
Hello.

00:03:22.334 --> 00:03:26.167
I have it tattooed on my back.
Absolutely.

00:03:26.167 --> 00:03:27.801
Congrats on the baby,
by the way.

00:03:27.801 --> 00:03:29.400
I know you have
a brand-new baby.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.133
-She's the cutest.
-Congratulations.

00:03:31.133 --> 00:03:33.434
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:03:33.434 --> 00:03:34.834
-It's the best thing
in the world.

00:03:34.834 --> 00:03:36.100
-The world. She just is smiling.

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:37.534
It just melts my heart
every day.

00:03:37.534 --> 00:03:39.400
-It's the best thing.
It'll change your life.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.167
It's the greatest thing
that ever happened.

00:03:41.167 --> 00:03:44.400
But it made you think of
this new training program.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:46.200
-Yes.
-Tell me about Strong4Me.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.834
-Well, it's just so hard
to get to the gym,

00:03:48.834 --> 00:03:51.367
leave the baby,
stop breast-feeding.

00:03:51.367 --> 00:03:53.200
And Strong4Me
is 30-minute workouts

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:54.634
you can do in your home.

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:56.400
12-week program

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:58.868
to make it obtainable
for anybody, any time.

00:03:58.868 --> 00:04:00.667
Limited equipment.

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:03.701
And I wanted to do it
for new moms, working moms,

00:04:03.701 --> 00:04:06.334
people to give them the access
to the workouts that I have,

00:04:06.334 --> 00:04:08.701
that I do to get ready
for "Sports Illustrated"

00:04:08.701 --> 00:04:11.934
and that I'm doing now to get
back to my post-baby weight.

00:04:11.934 --> 00:04:13.734
-And you're working with
a trainer to make this?

00:04:13.734 --> 00:04:17.467
-Yes, I'm working with
my trainer, Ben Bruno,

00:04:17.467 --> 00:04:19.033
who is a fantastic trainer.

00:04:19.033 --> 00:04:22.267
Completely changed my body and
how I thought about working out.

00:04:22.267 --> 00:04:24.000
-But you can do this stuff
at home?

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.434
-At home, 30 minutes.

00:04:25.434 --> 00:04:27.667
-Can I do something here
in commercial breaks?

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:29.300
'Cause the crowd knows, but
the people at home don't know.

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:31.501
I work out all the time.

00:04:31.501 --> 00:04:34.567
-I heard --
-I can't get enough of it.

00:04:34.567 --> 00:04:36.467
I mean, when I go
to commercial break,

00:04:36.467 --> 00:04:37.767
I don't want to waste any time.

00:04:37.767 --> 00:04:39.534
Could I do something with
the desk or something here?

00:04:39.534 --> 00:04:41.434
-Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah. We can
do something with the desk.

00:04:41.434 --> 00:04:42.701
You want to do it now?
-Yeah, sure.

00:04:42.701 --> 00:04:46.767
-I mean, I did hear that
you're just not very strong.

00:04:46.767 --> 00:04:48.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:49.901
-What?!
-So we could maybe --

00:04:49.901 --> 00:04:52.234
-You heard that?
-This could be your weight.

00:04:52.234 --> 00:04:54.133
-From someone that works here?

00:04:54.133 --> 00:04:56.634
-The whole -- Everybody.

00:04:56.634 --> 00:04:59.601
They were like, "Careful
with him. He's fragile."

00:04:59.601 --> 00:05:02.133
-I'm like a Fabergé egg.
I really am.

00:05:02.133 --> 00:05:04.934
-Lean against the desk. Get
into almost a plank position.

00:05:04.934 --> 00:05:07.000
And you can just start
doing rows.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:08.834
-Oh, this it?

00:05:08.834 --> 00:05:12.968
-Yeah, and if you get tired,
you only have to do three.

00:05:12.968 --> 00:05:14.234
-What are you talking about?

00:05:14.234 --> 00:05:15.501
I'm not even winded.
I'm barely winded.

00:05:15.501 --> 00:05:17.901
-This workout program
is for everyone.

00:05:17.901 --> 00:05:20.400
-So just lean against something.
-Yes.

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:22.634
-Grab some type of weight. But
what if I don't have a weight?

00:05:22.634 --> 00:05:24.801
Can I grab like -- I saw on
your thing like a soup can?

00:05:24.801 --> 00:05:26.300
-Oh, I think -- I mean,

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:28.400
I think some stronger people
could do that.

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:30.133
I'd be a little worried
about you.

00:05:30.133 --> 00:05:31.434
-Oh, my heavens. Come on.

00:05:31.434 --> 00:05:33.501
-Or, like, a jug of water
or, like, laundry detergent.

00:05:33.501 --> 00:05:35.000
-A jug of water?
Now you're talking.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:36.601
That's insane. Come on.
Give me a break.

00:05:36.601 --> 00:05:39.934
That sounds like torture.
I'm psyched for this.

00:05:39.934 --> 00:05:41.467
Kate Upton, congratulations

00:05:41.467 --> 00:05:42.701
on you and the baby
and Strong4Me.

00:05:42.701 --> 00:05:44.534
-Thank you so much.
-Kate Upton, everybody.

00:05:44.534 --> 00:05:47.467
Check out her new workout plan,
Strong4Me.

